config BR2_PACKAGE_LILSMOKE_FBTEST
    bool "lilsmoke-fbtest (framebuffer test app)"
    default y if BR2_PACKAGE_LILSMOKE_OS
    select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBPNG
    select BR2_PACKAGE_ZLIB
    help
      Tiny (~12 KB) framebuffer test app that:
        1. Opens /dev/fb0 and queries its geometry
        2. Loads assets/logo/lilsmoke-logo.webp OR a built-in fallback PNG
        3. Centers it on the framebuffer using direct mmap
        4. Prints the box dimensions and pixel format
        5. Waits 10 seconds, then exits

      This is the J1 smoke test for the fbdev stack. No SDL2, no
      DirectFB — just the raw Linux framebuffer API. Proves the
      kernel fbdev driver works before we stack anything on top.

      Build-time location: /usr/bin/lilsmoke-fbtest
      Runtime usage:      run from a tty (e.g. tty1)
